title: ERC-CUP government negotiations

See this? report a bug!

@erc_player_erc_led
title: <span class="generalitat-coalition" data-parties="erc cup" data-summary="Majority government - [+ parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s +]/[+ parlament_s_majority +]"><span style="color: var(--erc); font-style: italic;">ERC-led Left-Independence Government</span></span>
view-if: player_party = "erc" and erc_parlament_s >= cup_parlament_s and cup_parlament_s > 0
choose-if: parlament_erc_cup_government_available
unavailable-subtitle: ERC and the CUP need a majority, a shared independence roadmap, and enough mutual trust to govern together.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.erc_cup_coalition_phase = 1;
    Q.parlament_coalition_push = 0;
    Q.parlament_coalition_cabinet_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_support_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_leader = "erc";
    Q.parlament_coalition_follower = "cup";
    Q.speaker_party = "cup";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2017 ? "Julià de Jòdar" : "Vidal Aragonés";
    Q.speaker_gender = "m";
    Q.month_actions += 1;
!}

As the party that will hold the Presidency, ERC will lead the government negotiations. Before we present CUP with our opening cabinet proposal, the new Parlament must elect its Speaker. We are expected to nominate [+ speaker +] (CUP), leaving the Presidency and the position of the Speaker divided between the partners. Retaining both offices would reduce our leverage in the cabinet talks.

- @erc_leader_accept_cup_speaker
- @erc_leader_retain_speaker

@erc_leader_accept_cup_speaker
title: Nominate [+ speaker +] for Speaker
go-to: parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_erc_player_erc_led

@erc_leader_retain_speaker
title: Retain the Speakership for ERC
on-arrival: {!
    Q.speaker_party = "erc";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2016 ? "Anna Simó" : "Roger Torrent";
    Q.speaker_gender = Q.year < 2016 ? "f" : "m";
!}
go-to: parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_erc_player_erc_led

@erc_player_cup_led
title: <span class="generalitat-coalition" data-parties="cup erc" data-summary="Majority government - [+ parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s +]/[+ parlament_s_majority +]"><span style="color: var(--cup); font-style: italic;">CUP-led Left-Independence Government</span></span>
view-if: player_party = "erc" and cup_parlament_s > erc_parlament_s and erc_parlament_s > 0
choose-if: parlament_erc_cup_government_available
unavailable-subtitle: ERC and CUP need a majority, a shared independence roadmap, and enough mutual trust to govern together.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.erc_cup_coalition_phase = 1;
    Q.parlament_coalition_push = 0;
    Q.parlament_coalition_cabinet_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_support_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_leader = "cup";
    Q.parlament_coalition_follower = "erc";
    Q.speaker_party = "erc";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2016 ? "Anna Simó" : "Roger Torrent";
    Q.speaker_gender = Q.year < 2016 ? "f" : "m";
    Q.month_actions += 1;
!}

6H4 eCUP will hold the Presidency and lead the government negotiations. Its opening institutional proposal gives ERC the speaker before the CUP presents us with its cabinet offer.

- @parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_erc_player_cup_led: Accept [+ speaker +] as Speaker

