As the party that will hold the Presidency, the CUP will lead the government negotiations. Before we present ERC with our opening cabinet proposal, the new Parlament must elect its Speaker. We are expected to nominate [+ speaker +] (ERC), leaving the Presidency and Speaker of the House divided between the partners. Retaining both offices would reduce our leverage in the cabinet talks.

- @cup_leader_accept_erc_speaker
- @cup_leader_retain_speaker

@cup_leader_accept_erc_speaker
title: Nominate [+ speaker +] (ERC) for Speaker
go-to: parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_cup_player_cup_led

@cup_leader_retain_speaker
title: Retain the Speaker of the House for the CUP
on-arrival: {!
    Q.speaker_party = "cup";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2017 ? "Julià de Jòdar" : "Vidal Aragonés";
    Q.speaker_gender = "m";
!}
go-to: parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_cup_player_cup_led
